<title>GERMANY: German utility VEW details 1996 results.</title>
<headline>German utility VEW details 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>DORTMUND, Germany 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   281     vs 250</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   445     vs 489</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities    464     vs 427</p>
<p>    Group sales				  8,586   vs 8,546</p>
<p>by main sector</p>
<p>    -VEW Energy, MEAG			  7,390   vs 7,461</p>
<p>    -Waste disposal (Edelhoff)	     898     vs 873</p>
<p>    -Services (Harpen)			 298     vs 212</p>
<p>    Group income (DVFA)			400     vs 353</p>
<p>Group income net of minorities</p>
<p>    (DVFA)					 382     vs 330</p>
<p>    Earnings per share			 19.10   vs 16.49 marks</p>
<p>    Gross cash flow			    2,377   vs 1,986</p>
<p>    Net cash flow				2,185   vs 1,815</p>
<p>    Net interest income			(32)    vs (70)</p>
<p>    Net income from subsidiaries	   77	vs 34</p>
<p>    Capital expenditure			970     vs 1,255</p>
<p>    Staff costs				  1,668   vs 1,684</p>
<p>Electricity sales</p>
<p>    (millions of kilowatt hours)	   43,176  vs 43,616</p>
<p>Gas sales</p>
<p>    (millions of kilowatt hours)	   42,967  vs 37,831</p>
<p>District heating</p>
<p>    (millions of kilowatt hours)	   3,358   vs 2,576</p>
<p>    Employees (at 31.12.96)		  13,460  vs 13,178</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  250     vs 230</p>
<p>    Parent earnings per share		9.50    vs 9.00 marks</p>
<p>    Total dividend distribution	    190     vs 180</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German diversified utility group is VEW AG. Figures in brackets denote a loss. DVFA refers the DVFA German analysts' method.</p>
</text>
